  "report": "Implementation review passed; operator acceptance remains separate.\n\nRESULT: accepted\n\n**OBSERVED — candidate identity and scope.** HEAD is `a6ceb65a6682ac0048a6c20ae8e8ebc63f05306d`. `git status`, the staged and unstaged diffs, and file hashes match the delivered checkpoint: only the six allocated paths changed. `git diff --check` passed. This is acceptance of the slice candidate, not acceptance of the full requirements catalog.\n\n**Obligation assessment**\n- **RG-REQ-004:** RG-REQ-004-L03 meets this slice’s approved change: nested Gradle settings files produce declared module candidates, and the method label counts distinct settings-file evidence paths. RG-REQ-004-L01, RG-REQ-004-L02, RG-REQ-004-L04, RG-REQ-004-L05, RG-REQ-004-L06, RG-REQ-004-L07, RG-REQ-004-L08, RG-REQ-004-L09, RG-REQ-004-L10, RG-REQ-004-L11 and RG-REQ-004-L12 are preserved within the stated checks; the pre-existing `cycles`/`stats` population difference remains.\n- **RG-REQ-006:** RG-REQ-006-L01, RG-REQ-006-L02, RG-REQ-006-L03, RG-REQ-006-L04, RG-REQ-006-L05, RG-REQ-006-L06, RG-REQ-006-L07, RG-REQ-006-L08, RG-REQ-006-L09, RG-REQ-006-L10, RG-REQ-006-L11, RG-REQ-006-L12 and RG-REQ-006-L13 are preserved, not newly implemented by this slice.\n- **RG-REQ-002:** RG-REQ-002-L01, RG-REQ-002-L02, RG-REQ-002-L03, RG-REQ-002-L04, RG-REQ-002-L05, RG-REQ-002-L06, RG-REQ-002-L07, RG-REQ-002-L08, RG-REQ-002-L09, RG-REQ-002-L10 and RG-REQ-002-L11 are preserved within the bounded evidence, not claimed globally complete.\n- **P-DAP-01:** the old settings-relative parser remains unchanged. **P-DAP-02:** captured HEAD/candidate store diffs preserve files, nodes, edges and unresolved rows on hexmanos and rabbitmq-tutorials. **P-DAP-03:** the ownership test keeps a C file in its inferred group beside Java owned by a nested Gradle project. **P-DAP-04:** only the multi-settings Gradle method label changes. **P-DAP-05:** source inspection and the grpc-java capture support the stated path-keyed consumer